Description: Wild OS pop-ups: clipboard history and emoji
 The overlays Windows people reach for by shortcut:
 .
  * Win+V and Win+full stop: one panel for clipboard history (Klipper's,
    with pins that survive a restart), emoji and symbols, pasted straight
    into the app you were using.
  * The QML pieces the shell and Capture use for their toasts, on-screen
    displays and overlays: placing a window on a screen edge above
    everything, and Caps Lock and Num Lock state.
 .
 The clipboard history uses the private QML module of Plasma's clipboard
 widget, so it is tied to the Plasma version named in the dependencies.
